          { name: "Positioning as a Defender of Affluent Suburban Interests Without Acknowledging Broader Governance Obligations", tag: "avoid", why: "While college-educated affluent suburban voters are the primary electoral constituency in NJ-SD-16, a candidate whose entire positioning is property-tax relief and anti-regulatory rhetoric without any acknowledgment of broader governance obligations — healthcare equity, educational access for lower-income students, environmental stewardship beyond NIMBY preservation — will appear narrow and self-interested to the portion of the college-educated constituency motivated by institutional competence and public goods. The 66.8% college-educated figure includes substantial numbers of professionals who work in education, healthcare, and public service; positioning exclusively as the defender of affluent homeowner interests will alienate portions of the intended coalition." }
