          "Engage the Latino plurality with institutional fluency on economic mobility: the 37.3% Hispanic population is the district's largest demographic group and critical to both the 63% margin and Democratic durability; address workforce development, education quality, and wage growth with specificity to Latino families' economic stakes, not symbolic recognition.",
          "Hold the college-educated vote while building renter-majority power: the 31.8% college attainment and likely professional workforce support the Democratic base, but the 43.8% renter rate means younger adults and service-sector workers need evidence that government is delivering on their economic priorities; do not allow the educated vote to become comfortable at renters' expense.",
