          { name: "Dismissing Affluent Suburban Voters' Concerns as Illegitimate or Selfish", tag: "avoid", why: "In a district where the median household income is $133,644 and college attainment is 54.6%, framing voters' concerns about property taxes, school quality, or government efficiency as inherently selfish or as proxies for racial anxiety will alienate the actual constituency and reinforce a perception that an alternative candidate better understands their legitimate interests. Affluent, educated professionals — across racial and ethnic lines — have real governance concerns grounded in the material stakes of their asset holdings and their children's futures; engaging these concerns seriously, rather than dismissing them, is the minimum credibility threshold for any candidate in this district." }
