          { name: "Assuming Electoral Loyalty Without Active Community Presence", tag: "avoid", why: "At $53,325 median income with competing demands on time, money, and attention, working-class families in this district do not maintain continuous electoral engagement—they withdraw from political attention except at election time unless they perceive visible, ongoing responsiveness from their representative. A representative who campaigns actively but remains invisible in community institutions, constituent-service operations, and community-cultural spaces during non-election periods will find that 84% erodes as constituent connection weakens and competing messages gain influence." }
