          "Treat the multiethnic character as the district's governing reality, not a diversity talking point: the 39% white, 29% Asian, 21% Hispanic, and 7% Black populations together represent genuinely different economic interests, immigration experiences, and policy priorities — a representative who speaks to abstract equity rather than specific constituent concerns for each community will find the coalition fraying.",
          "Build constituent relationships grounded in transit access, walkability, and quality of life for renters: the 33.7-year median age, 72.6% renter rate, and high college attainment identify people who have chosen to live in an urban or inner-ring suburban environment and evaluate representation on whether government is improving that environment — not on partisan identity or inherited loyalty."
