          "Engage the district's racial and ethnic diversity with specificity and continuous visibility: the Black (38.3%), Hispanic (26.0%), white (25.2%), and Asian (6.4%) constituencies each have distinct civic institutions, community leaders, and constituency concerns that require direct engagement rather than generic minority outreach. A representative who moves fluidly among these communities, attends community events regularly, and addresses their specific concerns (employment access, police relations, school funding for predominantly minority schools) sustains the coalition foundation that produces 76%.",
          "Deliver concrete constituent services and municipal responsiveness: at a $79,866 income with 55.7% renters, the constituency depends on municipal services (transit, schools, sanitation, public safety) functioning effectively. A representative who can demonstrate rapid response to constituent complaints, coordinate with city agencies on service failures, and deliver visible improvements in neighborhood conditions is investing in the grassroots organizational infrastructure that prevents defection.",
