          { name: "Taking the 100% Result as a Durable Baseline Rather Than an Alignment to Be Maintained", tag: "avoid", why: "A 100% Democratic sweep is not a stable coalition — it is a snapshot of 2025 sentiment that must be actively maintained through measurable delivery on working-class economic security. Any Democratic incumbent who campaigns on the grounds that the seat is now 'safe' or who reduces constituent engagement and neighborhood presence will find that assumption falsified if a credible Republican challenger emerges with a compelling economic-security platform grounded in the district's actual household budget constraints and cost-of-living crisis." }
