          "Engage the majority-minority constituency (Hispanic/Latino 28.59%, Black 22.1%) with cultural and linguistic fluency and with concrete constituent service on the issues most pressing to each community — immigration enforcement impacts on mixed-status families, police accountability and neighborhood safety for Black residents, and economic mobility pathways for both communities are the substantive concerns, not generic appeals.",
          "Build a durable Democratic majority by treating the 40.9% renter constituency not as a voting bloc but as residents whose housing costs are consuming 30-40% of income and whose economic security depends on tenant protections, affordable housing development, and rent stabilization — concrete policy delivery on housing is the issue most likely to sustain Democratic alignment in this district.",
