          "Engage the professional-class homeowner majority (median income $103,650, 42% college-educated, 75.6% homeowners) on the specific governance and economic concerns that may have driven them toward Democratic candidates in 2025—tax fairness, education funding quality, local service delivery, or institutional competence. This cohort is persuadable and not inherently Democratic; understanding what they wanted from their representatives in 2025 is the foundation for any credible Republican pitch in 2027 or 2029.",
          "Build authentic relationships with the African American (22.65%), Hispanic (9.26%), and Asian (5.59%) communities—which together constitute 37.5% of the district—around their specific economic, healthcare, and educational priorities. The complete Democratic sweep suggests these communities either voted as a bloc for Democratic candidates or were not effectively engaged by Republican outreach; targeted community listening and issue-specific responsiveness are prerequisites for credible minority outreach.",
