          { name: "Dismissing Non-White Communities as Safe Democratic Votes", tag: "avoid", why: "The combination of 17.84% Hispanic, 11.95% Black, and 4.02% Asian populations, alongside a 61.99% white majority, means that non-white communities comprise over 34% of the district. These are not monolithic Democratic constituencies — they are diverse households with specific economic concerns around jobs, education, healthcare, and housing that cannot be assumed or taken for granted. A representative who consolidates the 100% result by delivering visibly on Hispanic and Black community concerns will hold the seat; one who assumes these voters have nowhere else to go invites a credible challenger who offers more attentive constituent service." }
