          { name: "Treating the 100% Democratic Sweep as a Temporary Swing", tag: "avoid", why: "A complete Democratic sweep of both seats in a district this affluent and educated is not a marginal shift — it is a sign of fundamental realignment in how this constituency evaluates Republican and Democratic governance. Republicans that approach this district as if one strong candidate and one election cycle will restore the old alignment are misdiagnosing the depth of preference change. The affluent, college-educated, 43-year-old homeowner base that should be reliably Republican instead chose Democrats across two separate races, indicating that rebuilding credibility will require sustained effort, specific local problem-solving, and demonstrated commitment to the issues this constituency actually cares about." }
