          { name: "Generic Partisan Messaging in a Competence-Driven District", tag: "avoid", why: "NJ-AD-24 is not a district where abstract partisan talking points — 'build the wall,' 'defund the police,' 'socialism vs. capitalism' — move voters. At 45% college attainment and $120K income, this is a constituency of professionals and business owners who think in terms of practical governance outcomes: Which candidate will manage local finances more competently? Who has a credible plan for school funding? How will they address healthcare costs? Any candidate relying on partisan rhetoric rather than specific policy answers will sound out of touch to a constituency that evaluates leaders as they would evaluate employees or vendors — on demonstrated competence and results." }
