          "Build visible, specific engagement with the 13.92% Hispanic/Latino community on workplace conditions, immigration and family protection, language access, and economic mobility; this constituency is meaningful enough to swing a competitive at-large race and has demonstrated capacity for swing behavior when perceiving direct candidate attention versus generic outreach.",
          "Treat the unopposed sweep as a vulnerability rather than a security: in a future competitive cycle, a candidate who cannot articulate specific legislative responses to the district's renter-majority economics and real constituent concerns will be vulnerable to a challenger who does, regardless of current partisan alignment."
